<title>PORTUGAL: Yield rises on Portugal 5-yr bonds.</title>
<headline>Yield rises on Portugal 5-yr bonds.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the result of the Portuguese Institute for Public Credit Management's auction of 25 billion escudos of five-year fixed-rate bonds (OT).</p>
<p>    ISSUER: Republic of Portugal   MATURITY: 23 March 2002</p>
<p>    AMOUNT PLACED: 25 bln esc	 COUPON: 5.75 pct</p>
<p>AVERAGE ACCEPTED YIELD: 6.42876</p>
<p>HIGHEST ACCEPTED: 6.43 LOWEST: 6.41</p>
<p>BIDS:  57.29 bln esc PAYMENT FREQUENCY: Annual</p>
<p>NOTES: The issue is fungible. The auction takes to 130.3 billion escudos the total amount of the bonds issued.</p>
</text>
